    "native": "<div class=\"slide-native sm-skill sm-check\" style=\"--accent:var(--aws-navy);\" data-correct=\"A,C\" data-multi=\"1\" data-rationale=\"When you configure the DynamoDB Encryption Client to use AWS KMS, the DynamoDB Encryption Client uses a KMS key that is always encrypted when the key is used outside of AWS KMS. This cryptographic materials provider returns a unique encryption key and a signing key for every table item. This method of encryption uses a symmetric KMS key. For more information about the Direct KMS Materials Provider that the DynamoDB Encryption Client uses, see Direct KMS Materials Provider. For more information about KMS keys, see AWS KMS Concepts.\" data-judge=\"{&quot;prompt&quot;: &quot;A company is developing a Python application that submits data to an Amazon DynamoDB table. The company requires client-side encryption of specific data items and end-to-end protection for the encrypted data in transit and at rest. Which combination of steps will meet the requirement to encrypt specific data items? (Select TWO.)&quot;, &quot;options&quot;: [&quot;When you configure the DynamoDB Encryption Client to use AWS KMS, the DynamoDB Encryption Client uses a KMS key that is always encrypted when the key is used outside of AWS KMS. This cryptographic materials provider returns a unique encryption key and a signing key for every table item. This method of encryption uses a symmetric KMS key. For more information about the Direct KMS Materials Provider that the DynamoDB Encryption Client uses, see Direct KMS Materials Provider. For more information about KMS keys, see AWS KMS Concepts.&quot;, &quot;When you configure the DynamoDB Encryption Client to use AWS KMS, the DynamoDB Encryption Client uses a KMS key that is always encrypted when the key is used outside of AWS KMS. This cryptographic materials provider returns a unique encryption key and a signing key for every table item. This method of encryption would require a symmetric KMS key, not an asymmetric key.&quot;, &quot;The DynamoDB Encryption Client provides end-to-end protection for your data in transit and at rest. You can encrypt selected items or attribute values in a table. For more information about DynamoDB client-side and server-side encryption, see Client-Side and Server-Side Encryption. For more information about the DynamoDB Encryption Client, see What Is the Amazon DynamoDB Encryption Client? For more information about how the DynamoDB Encryption Client works, see How the DynamoDB Encryption Client Works.&quot;, &quot;You can use this method for server-side encryption at rest. This solution does not meet the requirement for client-side encryption.&quot;, &quot;You can use this method for server-side encryption at rest. This solution does not meet the requirement for client-side encryption.&quot;], &quot;answer&quot;: &quot;When you configure the DynamoDB Encryption Client to use AWS KMS, the DynamoDB Encryption Client uses a KMS key that is always encrypted when the key is used outside of AWS KMS. This cryptographic materials provider returns a unique encryption key and a signing key for every table item. This method of encryption uses a symmetric KMS key. For more information about the Direct KMS Materials Provider that the DynamoDB Encryption Client uses, see Direct KMS Materials Provider. For more information about KMS keys, see AWS KMS Concepts.; The DynamoDB Encryption Client provides end-to-end protection for your data in transit and at rest. You can encrypt selected items or attribute values in a table. For more information about DynamoDB client-side and server-side encryption, see Client-Side and Server-Side Encryption. For more information about the DynamoDB Encryption Client, see What Is the Amazon DynamoDB Encryption Client? For more information about how the DynamoDB Encryption Client works, see How the DynamoDB Encryption Client Works.&quot;, &quot;why&quot;: &quot;When you configure the DynamoDB Encryption Client to use AWS KMS, the DynamoDB Encryption Client uses a KMS key that is always encrypted when the key is used outside of AWS KMS. This cryptographic materials provider returns a unique encryption key and a signing key for every table item. This method of encryption uses a symmetric KMS key. For more information about the Direct KMS Materials Provider that the DynamoDB Encryption Client uses, see Direct KMS Materials Provider. For more information about KMS keys, see AWS KMS Concepts.&quot;}\"><div class=\"kicker\">SESSION 3 &middot; KNOWLEDGE CHECK &middot; QUESTION 2 of 5</div><h2>Check yourself <span class=\"sm-check-hint\">select all that apply</span></h2><p class=\"sm-check-q\">A company is developing a Python application that submits data to an Amazon DynamoDB table. The company requires client-side encryption of specific data items and end-to-end protection for the encrypted data in transit and at rest. Which combination of steps will meet the requirement to encrypt specific data items? (Select TWO.)</p><div class=\"sm-opts\"><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"A\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">A</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">When you configure the DynamoDB Encryption Client to use AWS KMS, the DynamoDB Encryption Client uses a KMS key that is always encrypted when the key is used outside of AWS KMS. This cryptographic materials provider returns a unique encryption key and a signing key for every table item. This method of encryption uses a symmetric KMS key. For more information about the Direct KMS Materials Provider that the DynamoDB Encryption Client uses, see Direct KMS Materials Provider. For more information about KMS keys, see AWS KMS Concepts.</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"B\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">B</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">When you configure the DynamoDB Encryption Client to use AWS KMS, the DynamoDB Encryption Client uses a KMS key that is always encrypted when the key is used outside of AWS KMS. This cryptographic materials provider returns a unique encryption key and a signing key for every table item. This method of encryption would require a symmetric KMS key, not an asymmetric key.</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"C\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">C</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">The DynamoDB Encryption Client provides end-to-end protection for your data in transit and at rest. You can encrypt selected items or attribute values in a table. For more information about DynamoDB client-side and server-side encryption, see Client-Side and Server-Side Encryption. For more information about the DynamoDB Encryption Client, see What Is the Amazon DynamoDB Encryption Client? For more information about how the DynamoDB Encryption Client works, see How the DynamoDB Encryption Client Works.</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"D\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">D</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">You can use this method for server-side encryption at rest. This solution does not meet the requirement for client-side encryption.</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"E\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">E</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">You can use this method for server-side encryption at rest. This solution does not meet the requirement for client-side encryption.</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button></div><div class=\"sm-check-submit\"><button class=\"sm-submit\" type=\"button\" disabled>Submit</button></div><div class=\"sm-check-fb\" style=\"display:none\"></div><div class=\"sm-source\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-question\"></i> Knowledge check &middot; Exam Strategy Session 3 Answer Key</div></div>",
