    "native": "<div class=\"slide-native sm-skill sm-check\" style=\"--accent:var(--aws-navy);\" data-correct=\"C\" data-multi=\"\" data-rationale=\"Set the limit parameter to 1 to set the maximum number of items that need to be retrieved with a DynamoDB scan operation. For more information about limiting the number of the results in a scan, see Limiting the Number of Items in the Result Set.\" data-judge=\"{&quot;prompt&quot;: &quot;A developer uses the AWS SDK for C++ to retrieve data from an Amazon DynamoDB table. The data is sometimes retrieved using a known key, and sometimes the key is not known, resulting in multiple items being returned. The developer wants to ensure the code returns only one item when retrieving data without keys. Which DynamoDB setting will meet these requirements?&quot;, &quot;options&quot;: [&quot;The parallel scan operation can logically divide a table into multiple segments, with multiple application workers scanning the segments in parallel. Parallel scan returns the same number of results as an ordinary scan, except the results can be returned more quickly. Parallel scan does not limit the number of items returned. For more information about using DynamoDB parallel scans, see Parallel Scan.&quot;, &quot;A filter expression applies additional matching criteria to limit the items returned. This expression does not provide a specific limit on the number of items returned. For more information about using query filter expression statements in DynamoDB, see Query.&quot;, &quot;Set the limit parameter to 1 to set the maximum number of items that need to be retrieved with a DynamoDB scan operation. For more information about limiting the number of the results in a scan, see Limiting the Number of Items in the Result Set.&quot;, &quot;The page-size parameter will determine the number of items returned in each page of a query. This method is only relevant for queries that involve the key. For more information about queries in DynamoDB, see Working with Queries in DynamoDB. For more information about how to construct a query with pagination, see Paginating Table Query Results.&quot;], &quot;answer&quot;: &quot;Set the limit parameter to 1 to set the maximum number of items that need to be retrieved with a DynamoDB scan operation. For more information about limiting the number of the results in a scan, see Limiting the Number of Items in the Result Set.&quot;, &quot;why&quot;: &quot;Set the limit parameter to 1 to set the maximum number of items that need to be retrieved with a DynamoDB scan operation. For more information about limiting the number of the results in a scan, see Limiting the Number of Items in the Result Set.&quot;}\"><div class=\"kicker\">SESSION 3 &middot; KNOWLEDGE CHECK &middot; QUESTION 3 of 5</div><h2>Check yourself <span class=\"sm-check-hint\">click an option</span></h2><p class=\"sm-check-q\">A developer uses the AWS SDK for C++ to retrieve data from an Amazon DynamoDB table. The data is sometimes retrieved using a known key, and sometimes the key is not known, resulting in multiple items being returned. The developer wants to ensure the code returns only one item when retrieving data without keys. Which DynamoDB setting will meet these requirements?</p><div class=\"sm-opts\"><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"A\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">A</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">The parallel scan operation can logically divide a table into multiple segments, with multiple application workers scanning the segments in parallel. Parallel scan returns the same number of results as an ordinary scan, except the results can be returned more quickly. Parallel scan does not limit the number of items returned. For more information about using DynamoDB parallel scans, see Parallel Scan.</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"B\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">B</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">A filter expression applies additional matching criteria to limit the items returned. This expression does not provide a specific limit on the number of items returned. For more information about using query filter expression statements in DynamoDB, see Query.</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"C\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">C</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">Set the limit parameter to 1 to set the maximum number of items that need to be retrieved with a DynamoDB scan operation. For more information about limiting the number of the results in a scan, see Limiting the Number of Items in the Result Set.</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"D\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">D</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">The page-size parameter will determine the number of items returned in each page of a query. This method is only relevant for queries that involve the key. For more information about queries in DynamoDB, see Working with Queries in DynamoDB. For more information about how to construct a query with pagination, see Paginating Table Query Results.</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button></div><div class=\"sm-check-fb\" style=\"display:none\"></div><div class=\"sm-source\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-question\"></i> Knowledge check &middot; Exam Strategy Session 3 Answer Key</div></div>",
