    "native": "<div class=\"slide-native sm-skill sm-check\" style=\"--accent:var(--aws-navy);\" data-correct=\"B\" data-multi=\"\" data-rationale=\"Correct. DynamoDB is a NoSQL database that supports key-value records. DAX delivers response times in microseconds.\" data-judge=\"{&quot;prompt&quot;: &quot;Picking the right database option&quot;, &quot;options&quot;: [&quot;Incorrect. Aurora is a relational database (not a key-value database). Aurora is not likely to achieve microsecond latency consistently.&quot;, &quot;Correct. DynamoDB is a NoSQL database that supports key-value records. DAX delivers response times in microseconds.&quot;, &quot;Incorrect. Aurora is a relational database (not a key-value database). Aurora is not likely to achieve microsecond latency consistently, even with ElastiCache.&quot;, &quot;Incorrect. Neptune is a graph database that is optimized for working with highly connected data. Neptune is not optimized for simple key-value data.&quot;], &quot;answer&quot;: &quot;Correct. DynamoDB is a NoSQL database that supports key-value records. DAX delivers response times in microseconds.&quot;, &quot;why&quot;: &quot;Correct. DynamoDB is a NoSQL database that supports key-value records. DAX delivers response times in microseconds.&quot;}\"><div class=\"kicker\">SESSION 3 &middot; KNOWLEDGE CHECK &middot; QUESTION 5 of 5</div><h2>Check yourself <span class=\"sm-check-hint\">click an option</span></h2><p class=\"sm-check-q\">Picking the right database option</p><div class=\"sm-opts\"><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"A\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">A</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">Incorrect. Aurora is a relational database (not a key-value database). Aurora is not likely to achieve microsecond latency consistently.</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"B\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">B</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">Correct. DynamoDB is a NoSQL database that supports key-value records. DAX delivers response times in microseconds.</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"C\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">C</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">Incorrect. Aurora is a relational database (not a key-value database). Aurora is not likely to achieve microsecond latency consistently, even with ElastiCache.</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"D\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">D</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">Incorrect. Neptune is a graph database that is optimized for working with highly connected data. Neptune is not optimized for simple key-value data.</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button></div><div class=\"sm-check-fb\" style=\"display:none\"></div><div class=\"sm-source\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-question\"></i> Knowledge check &middot; Exam Strategy Session 3 Answer Key</div></div>",
